Looking at each intersection in the original drawing, every crossing point involves exactly two curve branches passing through each other (four branch ends), or a loop touching back at a crossing point. Sections A, B, D, and E each show such two‑strand crossings, matching the crossings at the top‑left loop, the middle loop, the top‑right loop, and the wave crossing.

Section C, however, shows three separate strands all passing through a single point (six branch ends meeting in one spot). In the original picture, the small loops near the center meet the passing curve at separate touching points – there is no place where three lines genuinely cross at one single point. Therefore C cannot be a magnified part of the picture.

\boxed{C}
